    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d781">

                <pb facs="0869" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/7–2545:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 781<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25T22:00:00+02:00">July 25, 1945—10 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3057. Msg (Message) from Potsdam to Chief of
                    Staff AFHQ<anchor n="1" xml:id="d781-f1"/>
                    (Allied Force Headquarters) advises that Stalin announced at session July 24<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d781-f2"/> that Marshal Koniev
                    (reference our 3000, July 20<anchor n="3" xml:id="d781-f3"/>) would continue to
                    provide food for whole of Vienna until an alternative arrangement can be agreed
                    with British and Americans. In view of above Field
                        Marshal Alexander directed that Commander Eighth Army assume
                    military government and occupational responsibilities for British sector of
                    Vienna as previously arranged. British Chiefs of Staff have assumed Americans
                    will do likewise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
